# Connector token for the Cloudflare tunnel — copy to
# secrets/cloudflared.env, fill in, then `./scripts/secrets encrypt`.
#
# Zero Trust dashboard -> Networks -> Tunnels -> Create a tunnel
# -> Cloudflared. Copy the token out of the install command it shows
# (the long string after `--token`), not the whole command.
#
# Then, on that tunnel's Public Hostname tab, add one entry:
#
#   Hostname : *.<your DOMAIN from .env>
#   Service  : HTTPS  ->  caddy:443
#   Additional settings -> TLS -> No TLS Verify: ON
#
# One wildcard entry is enough — cloudflared hands everything to Caddy
# and Caddy does the per-app routing, so routes live in one place. No
# TLS Verify is on because Caddy presents a cert for the public
# hostname while cloudflared connects to it by container name; the hop
# is container-to-container on the Docker bridge either way.
#
# Access policies attach per hostname under Access -> Applications.
# A hostname with a tunnel route but no Access policy is reachable by
# anyone who knows the name — the policy is the authentication.
TUNNEL_TOKEN=
